title: The Chancellery Grows
subtitle: Power is quietly moving to the Chancellor's office.
tags: event
view-if: date >= 30 and (pal_chancellor or puppet_chancellor) and not rc_chancellor
max-visits: 1
new-page: true
face-image: img/ev_chancellery.svg

= The Chancellery Grows

In the name of efficiency, the Chancellor's office has absorbed the staff of six Senate committees, the Senate Bureau of Intelligence's liaison office, and the Senate Guard's command. Each step was small and reasonable. Together they amount to a second government, answerable to [? if pal_chancellor : one man?][? if not pal_chancellor : one man, and he is not the Chancellor?]. [? if rc_in_govt : The Caucus sits in this government. Whatever it says now, it says from inside the cabinet room. ?]

- @resist: [? if rc_in_govt : Object inside the cabinet. ?][? if not rc_in_govt : Resist the transfers in committee. ?]
- @accept: Accept them. The Senate does need to work better.
- @transparency: Demand full transparency about who works for whom.

@resist
subtitle: −1 political capital. Slows the Chancellery's growth; it will be remembered.
choose-if: capital >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough political capital.
on-arrival: capital -= 1; grand_plan -= 2; pal_relation -= 6; senate_resolve += 0.3; bureau_captured = -1

[? if rc_in_govt : The Caucus's ministers refuse to sign the transfer orders, and several are quietly reversed. The Chancellor's office thanks its coalition partners for their "vigilance". ?][? if not rc_in_govt : The Caucus forces several transfers to be reversed. The Chancellor's office thanks the Caucus for its "vigilance". ?]

@accept
subtitle: Less gridlock, more power in one office.
on-arrival: corruption -= 2; grand_plan += 3; faith += 1; pal_relation += 3; bureau_captured = 1

The Senate becomes noticeably more efficient. Decisions that took years now take weeks, because they are no longer really being made by the Senate.

@transparency
subtitle: A little evidence; some resolve.
on-arrival: evidence += 0.4; senate_resolve += 0.3; pal_relation -= 2

The published staff rolls make interesting reading. A dozen names appear on no census of any world in the Republic.
